## Objective
- Follow `skills/AGENT.md` exactly and autonomously hunt/report high-impact vulnerabilities in authorized scope from `data/targets.txt`, writing all evidence/reports to `result/`.
- Target scope: `https://network.unifi.ui.com/6.1.71.0/unifi/site/default/dashboard` (single URL target); discover UI routes/API endpoints and test client-side + server-side bugs route-by-route.

## Important Details
- Repo root: `/home/runner/work/aaii-aautomattionn-for-doomainn/aaii-aautomattionn-for-doomainn`
- Target state: `decision=reset`, `run_id=41020096449`, `target_hash=05daa64f75198bf099bce7b5037a95c88aa4d275aa193003ab6486489ccc6e9b`.
- Creds in `creds/test-account.txt`: Account A `tan.tiger5564@maildrop.cc` / `Acd3423@#345`; Account B `overrated.chinchilla337@maildrop.cc` / `Acd3423@#345`. Both disposable/public.
- MFA codes retrieved via maildrop GraphQL: `POST https://api.maildrop.cc/graphql`; inbox query `query Inbox($mailbox:String!){inbox(mailbox:$mailbox){id subject date}}`; message query with `html` field (`text` field invalid).
- MFA entry: use `chrome-devtools_press_key` digit-by-digit; `fill`/`type_text` unreliable due to auto-advance. Email code prefix (e.g. `BQ`, `OO`, `CH`) matches page read-only prefix. After MFA choose `Not now` on trust-device prompt.
- App: UniFi Network AngularJS `6.1.71.0`, cloud/WebRTC mode. Both Account A and B have **no active console**: console errors `Option \`deviceId\` is required.`; page shows `Establishing Remote Connection` then `Connection failed.`
- App bootstrap fails before routing, so meaningful route logic/UI never renders; all data routes are unreachable.
- Same-origin API probes all return `502 Bad Gateway` (`server: awselb/2.0`): `/api/self`, `/status`, `/v2/api/self`, `/api/sso/v1/user/self`, `/api/airos/v1/unifi/devices/`.
- Static hosting: HTML served by `nginx`; missing files return S3 `AccessDenied` XML (`403`); unknown dirs return SPA index (`200`). Source maps `.map` return `403`.
- HTML response has no security headers: no CSP, HSTS, `X-Frame-Options`, `X-Content-Type-Options`, `Referrer-Policy` (possible clickjacking; low impact, not confirmed).
- `https://network.unifi.ui.com/6.1.71.0/unifi/fatal/404` redirected to `https://unifi.ubnt.com/6.1.71.0/unifi/fatal` → **out of scope**, record in `result/out-of-scope.txt`, do not test.
- `login?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fexample.com%2F` redirected to `/6.1.71.0/unifi/` (not external) → no open redirect observed.
- Google Analytics request leaked full URL incl. `/account/verify?email=test%40example.com&t=abc123` in `dl` param → possible sensitive token/email leak to GA; not confirmed high impact.
- Static analysis: 120 Angular ui-router state routes discovered; separate `when("...")` modal states also exist. Global `postMessage` service has `window.onmessage` with no origin check; only registered listener is `unifiIframePostMessage` requiring `{appLoaded:true}`; no sensitive effect observed.
- Do **not** create new accounts (two provided test accounts already exist; account creation is production side effect).
- Do **not** send Discord notification: no confirmed high-impact vulnerability.
- Do **not** add entries to `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` (no confirmed high-impact finding).
- `rg` not installed; use `grep -aoE` for minified bundles. `list_network_requests` rejects `websocket` resource type.
- Chrome MCP pages: page 1 default context = Account A authenticated (`/6.1.71.0/unifi/sites-overview`, connection failed); page 3 `isolatedContext=probe2` = Account B authenticated.
- Screenshot saved: `result/logs/evidence/connection-failed-accountA.png`.

